      license: "Public domain by age: photograph published in Buenos Aires in 1935, and Argentine copyright in photographs ran 20 years from publication (Law 11.723, art. 34), so it had expired before 1996 and was not restored in the United States. Caveats: the photographer is unnamed and the photograph's first publication may be earlier than this issue; the Biblioteca Nacional de Espana states that public-domain images on its site may be reused freely, but a search snippet also suggested that some of its Caras y Caretas items on Europeana carry a CC BY-NC-SA label (not opened, Europeana returned 403), which would concern the digitisation, not the 1935 photograph.",
