      // [src_ross_dsb, src_ross_nobel, src_ross_britannica, src_ross_smith2012 | 1881-1932 | reference biography, institutional biography, reference article, independent historical review] The sources document sustained work in medicine and parasitology, in mathematics (self-taught while in the Indian Medical Service; papers on pure and applied mathematics and epidemiological models), and in literature (plays, poems, fiction), with painting also noted. Independent scholarship confirms the mathematical output; the artistic output is described by the reference biographies and the Nobel text only. CONCENTRATION (agent): lowered from 72 / 0.58 to 70 / 0.54 because the arts side rests on reference-work biographies that draw on the same sources; only the mathematics is independently confirmed.
