      // [src_ross_dsb, src_ross_nobel, src_ross_britannica | 1897-1932 | reference biography, institutional biography, reference article] He wished as a youth to be an artist, published plays, short dramas, romances, fables and poetry that John Masefield approved, wrote the poem 'Exile' that includes verses written on 21 August 1897, and is called poet, playwright, writer and painter by the Nobel text. The sources document the output, not his taste or sensitivity as such, and none is independent of the others in kind. CONCENTRATION (agent): lowered from 68 / 0.52 (strong_inference) to 62 / 0.46 (inference) because one family of reference biographies documents the output and none speaks to taste or sensitivity.
      aesthetic_sensitivity: [62, 0.46, "i", "N"],
      // [src_ross_dsb, src_ross_capanna, src_ross_memoirs, src_ross_nobel | 1899-1902 | reference biography, partisan historical article, memoir, institutional biography] The DSB says a pugnacious streak often aroused hostility, the Nobel biography that his single-minded search for truth caused friction, and Capanna says that from late 1900 he campaigned publicly against Grassi and his colleagues over priority and accused Grassi of fraud; in his own chapter on the controversy he calls the Italian workers 'pirates' and writes that 'nothing new of fundamental importance was added'. The Grassi episode is the main evidence and Capanna is partisan. SELF-CALIBRATION (agent): top-risk row; lowered from 76 / 0.58 to 72 / 0.54 because the main episode (the Grassi dispute) is described by a partisan source and by his own memoir, while the DSB and Nobel phrases on his temperament are summary adjectives.
      conflict_tolerance: [72, 0.54, "s", "D"],
      // [src_ross_capanna, src_ross_memoirs | 1900-1902 | partisan historical article, memoir] The priority dispute shows a strong interest in being credited, and Capanna reads it as made with the Nobel Prize in prospect, which is an interpretation by a historian sympathetic to Grassi; Ross's own account claims the field's later work added nothing of fundamental importance. No independent source describes rivalry outside this episode. SELF-CALIBRATION (agent): lowered from 66 / 0.46 to 62 / 0.40 because the Nobel motive is Capanna's interpretation and the whole row rests on one episode.
      competitiveness: [62, 0.4, "i", "D"],
      // [src_ross_apte, src_ross_nobel, src_ross_smith2012, src_ross_dsb | 1895-1926 | memoir summary, institutional biography, independent historical review, reference biography] He pursued the mosquito hypothesis in India largely on his own initiative and, according to the summary of his Memoirs, spent considerable sums of his own; later he carried out surveys and prevention schemes in West Africa, the Suez Canal zone, Greece, Mauritius and Cyprus and set up anti-malaria organisations in the planting industries (Nobel biography), answered the failed Mian-Mir trial with a mathematical critique (Smith), and led the Ross Institute from 1926 (DSB). Most of the early self-funding detail comes from his own memoir. CONCENTRATION (agent): lowered from 72 / 0.56 to 68 / 0.52 because the early self-funding rests on a summary of his own Memoirs and the prevention-scheme list on the Nobel text drawn from his own account; Smith and the DSB are independent only for the Mian-Mir response and the Ross Institute.
      proactive_agency: [68, 0.52, "s", "A"],
      // [src_ross_dsb, src_ross_nobel, src_ross_smith2012 | 1888-1926 | reference biography, institutional biography, independent historical review] The DSB quotes his later reflection that he had asked what he had attempted towards bettering mankind by finding the causes of diseases; the Nobel text says his interest lay mainly in starting malaria-prevention measures in many countries, and Smith and colleagues describe his arguments for multi-pronged control, including its low cost relative to health benefits. The motive is documented chiefly by his own retrospective statement; his conduct (prevention work) is documented independently. CONCENTRATION (agent): lowered from 70 / 0.54 to 66 / 0.50 because the motive is his own retrospective statement quoted by the DSB; the independent evidence (Smith) documents conduct and cost arguments, not motive.
      impact_motivation: [66, 0.5, "s", "A"],
