      source: "Photograph of Shirase Nobu in army uniform with medals (photographer not named), printed in an oval on a plate of sixteen portraits with the printed caption 南極探険隊長たりし陸軍中尉 白瀬矗君 (Army Lieutenant Shirase Nobu, leader of the Antarctic expedition) and his Tokyo address, in the picture book Akita-ken shashin-roku (compiled by the Akita Photograph Exchange Society, Tsuchizaki-minato, Taisho 6 = 1917), digitised in the National Diet Library Digital Collections (item 1087219, page 23) and shown on the library's site Portraits of Modern Japanese Historical Figures. The image is the site's 421 x 821 pixel file, used as is: not resized and not upscaled.",
      license: "Public domain: photograph published in Japan in 1917 (before 1958, so its Japanese copyright had expired and was not restored in the United States); the National Diet Library item record carries the Public Domain Mark (rights code pdm, permission rule internet), and the library states that all images in the exhibition are in the public domain and may be reused including commercially",
