      // [src_tkk_roots, src_tkk_gacek, src_tkk_foundation, src_tkk_xiamengov | 1903-1950 | heritage story, scholarly article, foundation timeline, local-government profile] Roots says that when his father's businesses failed he worked to shut them down and clear the debts; Gacek and the foundation say that after the 1920s rubber price collapse he cut back Xiamen and Jimei building but that when his company collapsed in February 1934 he kept supporting the schools; the Xiamen government profile says he later funded their expansion with more than 10 million yuan by selling his Singapore property and raising donations. Several episodes, but all of them come from one biographical tradition and the later funding is described by promotional sources. SELF-CALIBRATION (agent): lowered from 74 / 0.58 to 70 / 0.52 because the episodes are repeated by sources that share one tradition and the funding totals come from promotional profiles.
