      // [src_tkk_gacek, src_tkk_roots, src_tkk_foundation, src_tkk_xmufounder | 1907-1954 | scholarly article, heritage story, foundation timeline, university profile] Gacek (via Yong) says he pledged one million dollars for Xiamen University's first two years and 250,000 dollars a year for twelve more, quotes Jamie Mackie's judgement that his primary aim was not simply to make money but to contribute to China's modernisation through education and new industries, and says he went on funding the schools after his firm collapsed; Roots says he reinvented himself to serve communities in Singapore and China and set up more than ten schools; the foundation and university profile list the schools and the 1918 Fujian normal school. The commitment is documented across 1907-1950s, but the strongest quotations come from admiring institutional or scholarly summaries of one biography. SELF-CALIBRATION (agent) and CONCENTRATION CHECK (agent): lowered from 80 / 0.6 to 74 / 0.54 because the supporting sources largely retell Yong and institutional hagiography, and a scholar's characterisation of motive is not independent behaviour. RUBRIC_CORRECTION (Roster67 lead review): 74@0.54 -> 72@0.5. every substantive source follows one tradition (Yong/NLB); no critical biography read.
      impact_motivation: [72, 0.5, "s", "A"],
      // [src_tkk_gacek, src_tkk_xmuarch | 1919-1921 | scholarly article, university feature] Gacek says that when planning Xiamen University he set aside a million dollars for the first two years and 250,000 dollars a year for the next twelve; the university's feature says he chose the site and set principles of economy, practicality, aesthetics and joining immediate needs to long-term vision. One funding plan from a secondary scholarly summary and one promotional institutional statement. CONCENTRATION CHECK (agent): lowered from 64 / 0.48 to 60 / 0.42 and reclassified from strong_inference to inference because the second item is promotional and neither describes his method.
      planning_orientation: [60, 0.42, "i", "A"],
      // [src_tkk_roots, src_tkk_gacek | 1920s-1954 | heritage story, scholarly article] Roots says his success was attributed to a fastidious nature and involvement in every stage of the supply chain, and Gacek says that in the 1950s he spent time planning, designing and inspecting the construction of school buildings and that twenty-four Xiamen University buildings completed in 1954 were personally designed by him. Both lines are second-hand characterisations drawn from other writers. CONCENTRATION CHECK (agent): lowered from 66 / 0.48 to 60 / 0.4 and reclassified from strong_inference to inference because one line is an attributed adjective and the other a scholar's summary of Yong.
      detail_orientation: [60, 0.4, "i", "A"],
      // [src_tkk_foundation, src_tkk_gacek, src_tkk_roots | 1907-1929 | foundation timeline, scholarly article, heritage story] He was among the founders of Tao Nan School in 1907, chaired the 1923-founded Ee Hoe Hean Club for Chinese businessmen, was elected president of the Singapore Hokkien Huay Kuan in 1929 and reorganised it (Gacek says he held the post until 1949), and chaired the Tientsin Flood Relief Fund of the Chinese Chamber of Commerce in 1917 (Gacek, foundation). Offices held show standing more than desire to lead, and the lists come from one biographical tradition. CONCENTRATION CHECK (agent): lowered from 68 / 0.5 to 64 / 0.44 because offices are not the same as the drive to lead and the sources repeat each other.
      leadership_drive: [64, 0.44, "s", "A"],
      // [src_tkk_biblioasia, src_tkk_gacek, src_tkk_foundation, src_tkk_roots | 1907-1921 | library-board article, scholarly article, foundation timeline, heritage story] He founded Tao Nan School together with 109 other Hokkien community members (foundation, Gacek), put Deng Cuiying and then Lim Boon Keng in charge of Xiamen University, Lim accepting his invitation in 1921 and running it for sixteen years (the NLB article on Lim, an independent source, and Gacek), and mentored Lee Kong Chian and Tan Lark Sye (Roots). The Lim invitation is independently confirmed; how he actually worked with others is not described. CONCENTRATION CHECK (agent): lowered from 62 / 0.46 to 58 / 0.42 because only one item is independent and none shows working practice.
